WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.440
We are going to put everything together for our full adult CPR scenario.

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:10.900
This is where you practice the complete path from the first moment of an emergency until

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:12.920
professional help arrives.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:18.719
In small groups, your instructor will assign clear roles so everyone knows their responsibility.

00:00:18.719 --> 00:00:24.719
One person will be rescuer one, focusing on giving breaths and operating the AED.

00:00:24.719 --> 00:00:28.080
Rescuer two will handle those critical chest compressions.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:33.200
If you have a third person, they can take over as the dedicated AED operator.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:38.320
We want every person in the group to rotate through each role so you leave here feeling

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:41.419
confident in every part of the rescue.

00:00:41.419 --> 00:00:45.840
Your instructor might choose to have multiple groups going at once, so don't be surprised

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:48.000
if the room feels a bit loud.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.020
We do this on purpose because a real world emergency is rarely a quiet or calm place.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:59.240
After the scenario is complete, your instructor will discuss performances and provide feedback.

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:02.860
They may also choose to do a repeat scenario for additional practice.

